EDG C++ front end -- C-CONVERTED FORK, TARGETED AT kencc
========================================================

This is NOT upstream EDG.  It is EDG's own C++ sources after being run
through EDG's own C-generating back end, with the back end configured
for APExp/kencc on amd64, so that a target with a C compiler and no
C++ compiler can build a C++ front end.

Upstream
--------
  https://github.com/edgcpp/compiler
  commit f0e30b65f  ("Implement full support for CWG 2355 (\"Deducing
  noexcept-specifiers\"). [GH #197]")

Licence
-------
  Apache License v2.0 with LLVM Exceptions.  LICENSE.txt is copied
  across verbatim from upstream and applies to everything here,
  generated or not.

Converted
---------
  Date:  2026-10-07   (round 2; round 1 of the same date is replaced)
  Host:  x86_64 Linux, gcc 13.3.0
  Tool:  cpfe built from the same commit, 23,113,832 bytes, via
           cmake --preset linux-gcc-release -B build/kencc \
                 -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-include <path>/kencc_targ.h"
           ninja cpfe
         kencc_targ.h IS COMMITTED BESIDE THIS FILE -- it is the one
         input to this directory that is neither upstream's nor
         generated, so a scratch copy of it would have made the whole
         translation unreproducible once the container went.
         It is the target configuration; see below.  It is a
         pre-included header rather than a patch: NOTHING IN THE EDG
         TREE IS MODIFIED.
  Driver: dev_tools/bin/eccp, with build/kencc/environment.sh sourced.

  src/     75 files   eccp -S --g++ --c++14 --no_exceptions --no_rtti
  util/     7 files   --clear_flag=use_predefined_macro_file
                      -DBACK_END_IS_C_GEN_BE=1
                      -DCOMPILE_MULTIPLE_TRANSLATION_UNITS=1
                      -DDO_IL_LOWERING=1 -DLOWER_IFUNC=1
                      -DNEED_IL_DISPLAY=1
                      -DRECORD_BACKING_EXPRS_WITH_IL_LOWERING=1
                      -DUSE_CMAKE_DEFINES
                      -DHOST_HAS_FLOAT16_TYPE=0
                      -DUSE_QUADMATH_LIBRARY=0
                      -DUSE_FLOAT128_FOR_HOST_FP_VALUE=0
                      -DFLOAT128_ENABLING_POSSIBLE=0
                      -DFLOAT80_ENABLING_POSSIBLE=0
                      -DFIXED_POINT_ALLOWED=0
                      -I<build>/src/includes -I<edg>/src
                      --no_standard_includes
                      --sys_include=<staged APExp amd64/include/ape>
                      --sys_include=<staged APExp sys/include/ape>
                      --sys_include=<edg>/include_c++
                      --sys_include=<edg>/include_c99
                      <file>.c
           (util/ adds -I<edg>/src; src/ is as written.)

  lib_src/ 51 files   eccp -S --building_runtime --c++23 --g++
                      -DUSE_STDINT_HEADER
                      -DSYSTEM_RUNTIME_HAS_IA64_THREAD_ATEXIT=0
                      --clear_flag=use_predefined_macro_file
                      (same four --sys_include, same order)

  Output is eccp's *.int.c renamed to *.c.  The only post-edit is a sed
  shortening the absolute scratchpad prefixes in the `# NNN "file"`
  line markers to `src/...`, `ape-arch/...` and `ape-sys/...`.

WHAT CHANGED FROM ROUND 1, AND WHY
----------------------------------
Round 1 proved the mechanism and was not a port.  Three things were
wrong with it, in descending order of importance.

1. IT EMITTED 26,712 `__attribute__((__weak__))`.
   Those are EDG's COMDAT emulation for vague linkage -- inline
   functions, template instantiations, vtables, typeinfo.  kencc has
   no weak symbols.
   The cause was not a flag anyone had set: targ_def.h:3505 infers
   GCC_IS_GENERATED_CODE_TARGET from `defined(__GNUC__)`, i.e. FROM
   THE COMPILER THAT BUILT cpfe, and that variable is the sole gate on
   both emission sites (c_gen_be.c:8806, :11103).  Built by g++, cpfe
   decided its output was for gcc.  Setting it to 0 selects
   targ_def.h's own "a compiler for which we have no special handling"
   arm, which is what kencc is.
   RESULT: 26,712 -> 0 applied.  See the attribute table below.

2. IT TARGETED LP64, NOT kencc.
   Round 1's output was for x86-64 Linux: `long` 8, `long double` 16.
   Measured, not assumed -- a probe translated through round-1 cpfe
   answered {char 1, short 2, int 4, long 8, long long 8, ptr 8,
   float 4, double 8, long double 16}.
   The same probe through this build answers
   {1, 2, 4, 4, 8, 8, 4, 8, 8}, plain char signed.

3. IT INLINED GLIBC'S HEADERS.
   eccp output is a whole preprocessed translation unit, so whichever
   libc's headers are on the path end up inside every .c file.  Round
   1 baked in /usr/include; this round uses APExp's own tree.  That is
   what removed the ~11,500 non-weak attribute sites: they were
   glibc's `__nothrow__`, `__always_inline__`, `__pure__` and the
   rest, not EDG's.

THE TARGET CONFIGURATION
------------------------
kencc on amd64 is LLP64, which is the integer model EDG already ships
as its **win64** configuration.  The values below were taken from that
configuration in the build's generated cmake_defines.h rather than
invented, and the three library types were read out of APExp's own
headers rather than inferred:

                        kencc   EDG win64   source
  char                      1           1
  short                     2           2
  int                       4           4
  long                      4           4   cc/sub.c; APE LONG_WIDTH 32
  long long                 8           8
  pointer                   8           8
  float                     4           4
  double                    8           8
  long double               8           8   kencc has no extended
                                            precision: cc/sub.c's
                                            simplet() maps
                                            BDOUBLE|BLONG to
                                            types[TDOUBLE]
  plain char            signed      signed  APE limits_generic.h:44,52
                                            CHAR_MAX == SCHAR_MAX
  endianness            little      little
  size_t       unsigned long long    same   stddef_arch.h:10
  ssize_t             long long     same    stddef_arch.h:14
  ptrdiff_t           long long     same    stddef_arch.h:4
  wchar_t          unsigned int  (u short)  stddef.h:50  <- the ONE
                                            place APExp and EDG's
                                            LLP64 config differ

Two settings are consequences of long-double-is-double rather than
choices.  floating.h:216 cross-checks the SIZE against the FORMAT, so
FP_LONG_DOUBLE_IS_BINARY64 has to replace the host's 80-bit extended
or the build stops with "long double type is mis-configured" -- the
check doing its job.  And at translation time the Plan 9 host has no
type wider than double, so __float128, 80-bit float and Embedded-C
fixed point are all off; each of those three was reported by its own
#error naming its own remedy, in that order.

`--clear_flag=use_predefined_macro_file` IS NOT OPTIONAL.  The build
generates a predefined-macro table by scraping the HOST g++, and it
hard-codes __PTRDIFF_TYPE__ = long int.  Against an LLP64 target that
is "incompatible redefinition of predefined macro __PTRDIFF_TYPE__"
and nothing translates at all.

WHAT IS HERE
------------
  src/      75 generated C files        133 files, ~2.90M lines, 160 MB
  lib_src/  51  (EDG's own runtime -- new/delete, vtbl, static init,
                 pure virtual, rtti.  NOT libstdc++.)
  util/      7  (decode, dettarg, edg_decode, edg_munch, edg_prelink,
                 make_win_predef_macro, mk_errinfo)
  include_c++/  EDG's own 17 headers, copied VERBATIM, not translated
  include_c99/  -- inputs cpfe hands to the programs IT compiles
  LICENSE.txt

NO HEADERS from upstream src/ are carried across and none are needed:
each .c here is a whole lowered translation unit and compiles with no
-I at all.

Deliberately absent: CMakeLists.txt, CMakePresets.json, cmake/,
src/cmake/, lib_src/cmake/, dev_tools/, benchmarks/, tests/, doc/,
dev_annex/, bases/, nt_util/, README.md, util/eccp.sh and the two
util/make_* shell scripts.

Absent because it will not translate:
  util/cfe_daemon_client.c -- the only file in the tree that needs a
  real C++ standard library:
      src/cfe_daemon_common.h, line 80: catastrophic error: cannot
      open source file "cstddef"
  It is the unix-domain-socket client for the compile daemon, so it is
  out of scope for Plan 9 twice over.  src/cfe_daemon.c (the server
  side) translates: its use of those headers is behind a guard.
  Unchanged from round 1.

MKFILES EXIST NOW -- sys/src/ape/lib/edg (libedg.a, mksyslib, 51
files) and sys/src/ape/cmd/edg (cpfe, mkone, 75 files).  Neither is in
sys/src/cmd/mkfile's lists, deliberately: one failing entry aborts the
whole tree's mk.  Build lib/edg first and with `mk -k'; each mkfile's
header says why.  util/'s six binaries have no mkfile and block
nothing.

WHAT KENCC IS AND IS NOT EXPECTED TO REFUSE
-------------------------------------------
Swept over all 133 files with COMMENTS, STRING AND CHARACTER LITERALS
AND `#line' STRIPPED FIRST, which is the whole measurement rather than
a tidying step: a raw grep reports `alignof' 2343 times, `typeof' 425,
`static_assert' 1156 and `_Complex' 702, and after stripping every one
of those is ZERO.  They were EDG's own diagnostic text and its own
mangled names -- `_ZN3edg27ec_wrong_entity_for_alignasE',
`_ZN3edg16ec_static_assertE' -- i.e. the word inside a longer
identifier, never a keyword.  (Two different word-boundary mistakes of
mine produced those numbers before the stripping did; the same trap as
counting `bool'/`nullptr' in round 1.)

  ZERO, after stripping:  __attribute__, asm/__asm, ({...}) statement
  expressions, __builtin_*, inline/__inline, restrict/__restrict,
  _Complex, _Imaginary, _Atomic, _BitInt, _Decimal*, __int128,
  _Alignas, _Alignof, alignas, alignof, typeof, _Static_assert,
  static_assert, _Generic, _Noreturn, _Thread_local, nullptr,
  constexpr, computed goto, #pragma, wide/UTF string literals,
  __label__, designated initializers, anonymous struct/union members,
  VLAs, K&R definitions.

  NOT zero in three files, and `mk -k install' ON THE VM HAS NOW
  ANSWERED: 50 of lib_src/'s 51 compile and ONE does not.

      lib_src/c99_complex.c   _Float16, __bf16, __float80, __float128
          FAILS, predicted by name and by token:
          `<noname>:42[stdin:45] syntax error, last name: _Float16'
          It is the C99 `_Complex' runtime and builds its own
          `struct _Complex_float16 { _Float16 _Vals[2]; }'.  Those are
          gcc's extended floats and they bring libgcc's soft-float
          family with them (__addtf3, __multf3, __eqhf2, ...), so the
          file is twice out of reach.  Commented out of lib/edg's
          OFILES now that the measurement is taken: a C++ front end
          has no use for a _Complex runtime.

      lib_src/thread_dtor.c   __thread  -- COMPILES
      lib_src/dtor_list.c     __thread  -- COMPILES

  **THE TWO `__thread' PREDICTIONS WERE WRONG, AND THAT IS THE MORE
  USEFUL HALF OF THE RUN.**  I checked EDG's constructs against C
  dialects FROM MEMORY instead of against the compiler in this
  repository, where `cc/lex.c:1765' has carried `"__thread", LNAME, 0'
  and a swallow at `:1095' all along, under the comment *"Plan 9 has
  no TLS; silently drop the qualifier."*  *An instrument whose keyword
  list is not the COMPILER's keyword list is measuring a different
  compiler* -- the include-path lesson apdecl-sweep and apehdr-sweep
  each paid for, arriving one level down for a lexer.  The list to
  check against is `itab' plus that swallow list, both in the tree,
  and checking the four float types against it afterwards is what says
  c99_complex.c really is the only failure.

  AND THAT PASS IS NOT A CLEAN BILL.  `__thread' dropped means
  `__thread_needed_destruction_head' is one process-wide global shared
  by every thread rather than one per thread -- this tree's commonest
  bug shape, a stub answering the wrong thing rather than "nothing to
  do".  Harmless for cpfe, which is single-threaded; a live hazard for
  anything else cpfe ever translates.  Recorded, not fixed.

  `gcc -fsyntax-only' could not have reported any of this, and the
  reason is worth keeping: every one of these is a feature of the HOST
  COMPILER rather than of EDG's design, so *the host compiler is
  exactly the one that put them there.*

  SIZE LIMITS asked rather than assumed, because a 315,616-line
  translation unit invites them, and none bites:

      longest line                430 bytes   (cpp INS is 32768)
      lines over cpp's OBS 4096   0
      longest identifier          295 chars   (cc's NSYMB is 1500)
      longest string literal      131 chars
      most `case' in one file     7204        (6c's Case is a LIST)
      6c's NSYM 50                NOT a cap -- swt.c:229 wraps the
                                  slot to 1 and re-emits the ANAME,
                                  so it is a cache, not a wall

  And one thing the sweep CONFIRMED rather than found: nine of src/'s
  files carry `extern unsigned char _ctype[];', byte for byte what
  APE's own <ctype.h> declares -- so the staged headers really were
  this tree's and not glibc's, independently of this file saying so.
  It also pins the generated C to this tree's `_ctype' BIT LAYOUT,
  which the _ISblank round changed: changing it again costs a
  re-translation.

